{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RX5YcBp1xj3xo47N458Fyo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives specifications from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies output parity via differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go binaries), `pkg/sys/` (Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (column alignment, ANSI color, human-readable sizes), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists for `pkg/testutils/` (with tests), `pkg/format/` (with tests), and `pkg/sys/` (without tests). No `cmd/` utilities exist on the working branch. Specs are complete for releases 00.0 through 01.3 and deferred releases 99.x.\n\n**Current release**: Release 00.0 (\"Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure\") with four use cases: uc001-magefiles (cmd/version), uc002-format (code exists), uc003-sys (code exists, **no tests**), uc004-testutils (code and tests exist).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Of its four use cases:\n- uc002-format: code + tests exist in source_code → done\n- uc004-testutils: code + tests exist in source_code → done\n- uc003-sys: code exists but **no test files** in source_code → gap\n- uc001-magefiles: cmd/version not yet implemented\n\nThe clearest gap is `pkg/sys/` tests. The implementation exists (terminal.go, fileinfo.go, platform files) but has zero test coverage. Per P8, tests follow implementation — and the implementation is already present.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd002-sys R1, R2 -- unit tests for pkg/sys terminal and file metadata\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (requirements R1 and R2)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (TerminalSize implementation -- prd002-sys R1.1, R1.2)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (Lstat and FileInfo struct -- prd002-sys R2.1, R2.2)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go (Darwin fillFromStat -- prd002-sys R2.3)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go (Linux fillFromStat -- prd002-sys R2.3)\n      - pkg/format/color_test.go (test style reference for this project)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go (test patterns used in this project)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for TerminalSize (prd002-sys R1.1, R1.2)\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for Lstat and FileInfo (prd002-sys R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test TerminalSize returns an error when stdout is not a TTY (prd002-sys R1.1, R1.2). Create an os.Pipe, and verify that calling the ioctl on a pipe fd returns an error. Do not test the TTY success path in CI since there is no guaranteed TTY -- only verify the non-TTY error path.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test Lstat populates FileInfo fields for regular files, directories, and symlinks (prd002-sys R2.1, R2.2). Create fixtures in t.TempDir, call Lstat on each, and verify Mode, Size, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Ino, and ModTime are populated with plausible values.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test Lstat returns an error for nonexistent paths (prd002-sys R2.1). Call Lstat on a path that does not exist and verify the error is non-nil.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test FileInfo.Blocks and FileInfo.Blksize are populated for regular files on the current platform (prd002-sys R2.2, R2.3). Create a file with known content via os.WriteFile, call Lstat, and verify Blocks > 0 and Blksize > 0.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use t.TempDir for all filesystem fixtures so cleanup is automatic.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Test files use package sys (not sys_test) to match the white-box testing convention used in pkg/format/ and pkg/testutils/.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Each test file has the copyright header and SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT matching existing source files in the project.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/sys/ passes on Linux.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"terminal_test.go covers the non-TTY error path for TerminalSize.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"fileinfo_test.go covers Lstat for regular files, directories, symlinks, and nonexistent paths.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"fileinfo_test.go verifies that Nlink, Uid, Gid, Ino, Blocks, Blksize, and ModTime are populated for a regular file.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/ reports no issues.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42102,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42102},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"09eb1402-c333-43f0-b077-7b0d5b8210be","uuid":"2a7b9a8d-f7cf-4f3b-befb-e670d6f6de4b"}
